{
  "@context": "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Article",
  "@id": "urn:etzhayyim:news:gow-ragnarok-berserkers-complete-guide-2026",
  "identifier": "gow-ragnarok-berserkers-complete-guide-2026",
  "headline": "God of War Ragnarok: All Berserkers Guide (12 bosses + King) with a stability-first strategy",
  "description": "A complete, repeatable plan for the Fit for a King Berserker Gravestones: universal combat rules, multi-boss fight handling, and concise notes for every Berserker plus King Hrolf.",
  "articleBody": "This guide is designed to help you clear every Berserker fight in God of War Ragnarok with consistency. Instead of chasing one perfect build, the goal is to standardize: (1) a universal win condition, (2) a reliable way to handle 2-boss and 3-boss fights, and (3) a fixed set of notes per boss: threat, punish window, spacing plan.\n\n0. The full scope\n- There are 10 Berserker Gravestones.\n- Two of them are multi-boss encounters (2 bosses, 3 bosses).\n- That makes 12 Berserker bosses total.\n- After defeating them all, King Hrolf Kraki unlocks, for 13 boss fights overall.\n\n1. Gravestones index (where and who)\nUse this as a navigation index.\n- Svartalfheim (Alberich Hollow): Fraekni the Zealous\n- Svartalfheim (The Applecore): Hardrefill the Callous\n- Svartalfheim (Sverd Sands / The Pitmines): Bodvar the Fierce + Starolfr the Troublesome\n- Vanaheim (The Sinkholes): Hjalti the Stolid\n- Vanaheim (The Jungle): Haklangr the Bearded\n- Vanaheim (The Plains): Hvitserkr the Bold\n- Alfheim (The Forbidden Sands / The Barrens): Svipdagr the Cold + Hromundr the Cruel + Vottr the Prideful\n- Midgard (King’s Grave): Beigadr the Feared\n- Niflheim (Mystic Gateway): Skjothendi the Unerring\n\nNote: Niflheim access and several Vanaheim sub-areas depend on story progression and area unlocks.\n\n2. Universal rules (the fastest way to raise win rate)\n- Unblockables first: decide your dodge direction and spacing before committing to damage\n- Do not get greedy: one safe punish then reset beats long strings on higher difficulty\n- Fix your defense style: mostly parry or mostly evade; mixing too much slows reactions\n- Cooldowns should be “reliably landable”: prefer short, consistent runics over flashy long animations\n- Have a reset move: create space, re-center the camera, put all threats back on screen\n\n3. Multi-boss handling (2-boss and 3-boss fights)\n- Camera is a mechanic: reposition until you can see multiple threats at once\n- Target selection: hit the safest target, not the one you wish you could hit\n- Priority: stop ranged pressure and summon/zone tools first\n\n4. Boss notes (all of them)\nEach boss should be learned with a small set: threat, punish, spacing.\n\nFraekni the Zealous\n- Threat: aggressive melee strings, unblockable gap-closers\n- Punish: end of sweep strings, recovery after lunges\n- Spacing: mid-range, dodge laterally on red attacks to create back hits\n\nHardrefill the Callous\n- Threat: guard-breaking greatsword pressure, unblockable jump slam\n- Punish: after the slam landing, after heavy swing follow-through\n- Spacing: prefer evasion to forced parry when the chain is breaking guard\n\nBodvar the Fierce + Starolfr the Troublesome\n- Threat: Bodvar’s rapid punches and AoE, Starolfr’s aerial dive patterns\n- Punish: landings (dives), end of rush strings\n- Spacing: never lose one boss off-screen; when it gets messy, create time to reset\n\nHjalti the Stolid\n- Threat: dual-mace pressure, slam shockwaves, daze AoE\n- Punish: after slam/shockwave sequences\n- Spacing: do not over-commit in close range; interrupts can help reclaim tempo\n\nHaklangr the Bearded\n- Threat: wide hammer arcs, delayed slams that catch early dodges\n- Punish: after committed big swings\n- Spacing: wait out delays, then dodge; swap weapons correctly if an elite bar is involved\n\nHvitserkr the Bold\n- Threat: poison pressure plus summons (Reavers/Nightmares) that ruin visibility\n- Punish: right after summon animations, after poison-heavy actions\n- Spacing: clear adds first to restore camera control and safe healing windows\n\nSvipdagr the Cold + Hromundr the Cruel + Vottr the Prideful\n- Threat: constant fire/ice projectiles from the sisters plus Svipdagr’s melee forcing bad dodges\n- Punish: after projectile volleys, after Svipdagr’s big committed swings\n- Spacing: sisters first is usually safest; reduce ranged pressure, then stabilize the melee duel\n\nBeigadr the Feared\n- Threat: lightning ranged pressure, teleports, immobilizing fist-style attacks\n- Punish: end of teleport strings, after major lightning casts\n- Spacing: prioritize tracking and visibility over forcing melee; pre-plan your dodge angle for immobilize threats\n\nSkjothendi the Unerring\n- Threat: Bifrost pressure, fast fist entries, aerial drops\n- Punish: after aerial landings, after Bifrost-heavy moves\n- Spacing: do not let Bifrost accumulate; punish once, then reset\n\nKing Hrolf Kraki\n- Threat: a composite fight that mixes Berserker patterns; Bifrost and elite-style pressure can snowball mistakes\n- Punish: after major specials and committed gap-closers\n- Spacing: stability over burst; remove your main failure mode, and win with safe confirms\n\n5. Recommended clear order\n- Clear single-target gravestones first to lock fundamentals.\n- Then do the 2-boss fight, then the 3-boss fight.\n- Finally, fight King Hrolf.\n\nThis order reduces the chance that multi-boss fights break your rhythm before your fundamentals are stable.",
